{"assets":["/editorial-assets/6abc1f2781b5d6b1e8df9c0df04229a65ef3c5b40b2eed84c84ffcc0f7eaf608.png","/editorial-assets/d0e2bb0b3a3e3b4acb3088bf605635010ec6315eefe362938aabbc681c3c7ef3.png","/editorial-assets/f9edda04d142988747c93c4e7ffb9141d5687b7dd90520c29948f28573b3d1a1.png","/editorial-assets/d2f89bf8c66d7f1883442c8192db04a33520d187115c013fce56c289817a8e7b.png","/editorial-assets/ef8ba4f90f3321e695024cec9ecf35dd7760abe17c69e251f7fc7ce3326bc7f7.png","/editorial-assets/d7960c9c55d089a4e055242e46526f8887297dfef9958f5a74fdbef38d80ecec.png"],"contestId":"878","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Div 2 A"}]},"children":[{"attrs":{"problemCode":"879A"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/879/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"879A - Borya's Diagnosis"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that Borya can use a greedy algorithm. He will visit each doctor as soon as possible. We only need to find the earliest day when he can do it. Constraints are pretty low, so we can use almost any reasonable way."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, we can just go through all the days, starting from the current one, and check if the doctor is working on that day. At the step "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" we need to go through at most "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"max"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") days."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There is a more efficient way. We can find the smallest "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" that is greater than the current day, such that "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/6abc1f2781b5d6b1e8df9c0df04229a65ef3c5b40b2eed84c84ffcc0f7eaf608.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(1). If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≥ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", Borya will visit a doctor on day "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", otherwise on day "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":". This solution is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Div 2 B"}]},"children":[{"attrs":{"problemCode":"879B"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/879/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"879B - Table Tennis"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It's not very difficult to solve this problem in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). The statement hints us that we can use the data structure queue. We need to maintain the queue of players, the current winner and the number of wins he has. Each game is processed in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(1). It can be shown that number of games is less than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Of course, this solution is too slow. Let's think what happens if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is large. More precisely, assume that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≥ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1. The winner need to win at least "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 games in a row, that is, he need to win against all the other players. Hence, the winner is just the strongest player."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So, if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≥ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1, we can solve the problem in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(1). Otherwise simulation works in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Div 2 C = Div 1 A"}]},"children":[{"attrs":{"problemCode":"878A"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/878/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"878A - Short Program"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's see what happens with a single bit. All operations work with each bit separately, so each bit of output depends only on the corresponding bit of input."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are only four options: bit doesn't change, bit always changes, bit is set to 0, bit is set to 1. For each bit it's easy to find which of these options happens to it."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now let's write a program of three lines: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Use XOR with a number that has ones in bits that must be reversed. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Use OR with a number that has ones in bits which must be set to 1. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Use AND with a number that has zeroes in bits that must be set to 0. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" It's easy to see that this program is equivalent to Petya's program."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Depending on the implementation, it may works in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") or "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/d0e2bb0b3a3e3b4acb3088bf605635010ec6315eefe362938aabbc681c3c7ef3.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"BONUS: solve a problem using at most two commands."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Div 2 D = Div 1 B"}]},"children":[{"attrs":{"problemCode":"878B"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/878/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"878B - Teams Formation"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"First, let's see what happens inside one bus. We can use a stack containing pairs (city, number of participants from it). When the number of participants reaches $$$k$$$, we erase the pair."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Suppose we build this stack. $$$r$$$ is its size, $$$(c_i, d_i)$$$ are pairs in it. Now consider the interaction of two such buses. At the border, a team is formed, if $$$c_1 = c_r$$$ and $$$d_1 + d_r \\ge k$$$. If the inequality becomes an equality, then another team can be formed from the second and penultimate groups, etc. Let's find the greatest $$$p$$$ such that for each $$$i = 1 \\ldots p$$$ we have $$$c_i = c_{r+1-i}$$$ and $$$d_i + d_{r+1-i} = k$$$. Since the condition on $$$i$$$ is symmetric with respect to $$$i \\mapsto r+1-i$$$, if $$$p \\ge \\lceil r / 2 \\rceil$$$, then $$$p = r$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider the case $$$p = r$$$ separately. This means that the two buses are completely divided into teams. If $$$m$$$ is even, answer is zero, otherwise answer is the sum of $$$d_i$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Also, consider the case when $$$r$$$ is odd and $$$p = \\lfloor r / 2 \\rfloor$$$. In this case, after removing all teams at the borders of the buses, the queue looks like: left part of the first bus — $$$m d_{p + 1}$$$ people from the $$$c_{p + 1}$$$ city — right part of the last bus. If the number of people in the middle is divisible by $$$k$$$, then they will be divided into the commands, and the first half will unite with the last, and the answer is zero. If it doesn't, then some teams will be formed in the middle, and the process will end there."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Finally, if $$$r$$$ is even smaller, it can be seen that after the formation of teams at the borders of buses the process will end."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Div 2 E = Div 1 C"}]},"children":[{"attrs":{"problemCode":"878C"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/878/problem/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"878C - Tournament"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Imagine a directed graph, in which the vertices are participants, and the edge means that one participant can win the other in some kind of sports. A participant can win a tournament if there is a directed tree in this graph that contains all vertices, and this player is a root."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider the condensation of this graph. Since for any two vertices there is an edge at least in one direction, condensation is a path. It is clear that the required tree exists if and only if the root lies in the first strongly connected component."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We will maintain these strongly connected components. For each of them we will store its size, the greatest power and the smallest power in each kind of sports."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"What happens when the new sportsman is added? He can defeat the component if in some kind of sports he is stronger than the minimum in this component. Similarly, he can lose to a component if in some kind of sports he is weaker than the maximum in this component. We need to find the weakest of those components that he can lose, and the strongest of those components that he can defeat. If the first component is stronger than the second, the new sportsman forms a new component. Otherwise, all the components between the first and the second merge into one, and the new sportsman joins it."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"How to do it effectively? We will store the components in a some search tree and use the comparison by minimum in the first kind of sports as a comparator. It's easy to see that if you take any other sport or replace a minimum with a maximum, any two components will be compared in the same way. All we need is binsearch by one of the mentioned comparators: minimum or maximum for one of the kinds of sports."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"At each step the number of operations with the tree is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"· number of components merged into one. At each step at most one component can be added, so the amortized time of one step is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/f9edda04d142988747c93c4e7ffb9141d5687b7dd90520c29948f28573b3d1a1.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Overall time complexity is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/d2f89bf8c66d7f1883442c8192db04a33520d187115c013fce56c289817a8e7b.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Div 1 D"}]},"children":[{"attrs":{"problemCode":"878D"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/878/problem/D"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"878D - Magic Breeding"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's consider a special case of the problem: all "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ij"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" are 0 or 1. In this case there are at most 2"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" different characteristics. So we can use trivial solution, it works in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"q"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"2"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Also we can sped up it using bitset."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now we reduce the problem to this special case. We have a characteristic with values "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ ... ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":". Let's make "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" characteristics from it. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th of them is one if and only if the original characteristic is at least "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", and zero otherwise. New characteristics behave correctly during our operations, and we can efficiently get old characteristics from them."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Number of characteristics has increased, but is doesn't matter for our solution for the special case. This solution works in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"q"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"2"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Div 1 E"}]},"children":[{"attrs":{"problemCode":"878E"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/878/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"878E - Numbers on the blackboard"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's find a strategy for Sasha. His result can be represented in the form "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/ef8ba4f90f3321e695024cec9ecf35dd7760abe17c69e251f7fc7ce3326bc7f7.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 0, 1 ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1 for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" > 1."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For all "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" satisfying these conditions he can obtain such result. We prove this by induction. For "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1 is't obvious. Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" > 1. Find the greatest "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" such that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1. It always exists cause "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1. By the induction hypothesis we can get "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"... "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1... "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1. Do this and merge them with the last move."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now we describe the strategy. Let the last number be negative. Then Sasha wants to minimize "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":". He always can use "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1. If tha last number is non-negative, he can use "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1. In this case, Sasha first merges the last two numbers. Thus, the sequence "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" consists of several blocks, in each of which "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1, and each of the blocks except the first begins with 1."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now we need to answer queries. We will do it offline. On the step "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" add the number "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" and and answer all queries with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". We will support the blocks for the query [1, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"What happens when we add a number? If it's negative, it simply forms a separate block. Otherwise it becomes the end of some block. It is easy to see that the new block is the union of several old blocks."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"How to answer queries? ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] is the union of some blocks and a suffix of another block. We can see that this is the partition into blocks for our query."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"How to do it fast? We will store the boundaries of blocks to do binary search on them and find the block in which the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" lies. We need to store the results for each block and prefix sums of these results. Also we need to find sums "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/d7960c9c55d089a4e055242e46526f8887297dfef9958f5a74fdbef38d80ecec.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" to find out results for suffixes."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each step is processed in "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/f9edda04d142988747c93c4e7ffb9141d5687b7dd90520c29948f28573b3d1a1.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" except for merging blocks. But we create at most one block on each step, so amortized time of each step is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/f9edda04d142988747c93c4e7ffb9141d5687b7dd90520c29948f28573b3d1a1.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Also in this problem we need to be careful with overflows. Although we need to find the result modulo some prime, in some places the sign is important. We can use that if |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| is more than maximum "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", then "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 2"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is also big and have the same sign."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"BONUS: solve this problem online."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"БОНУС: solve it in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"α("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"))."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"}],"kind":"spoiler"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/55435"}